From 03b42954805c6261c29c752fac3e9cc31a2e1db8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:37:49 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] NLHAL: stabilize MLO BSS registration and ownership

Wait for kernel and hostapd to register newly added BSSes before using them for MLO operations, and accept valid DFS/CAC states during VAP credential updates.

Filter refresh and monitor events to the local MLO link, use STATUS indices when rebuilding the VAP map, and prevent stale mld_ap state for non-MLO BSSes. Skip VAP DB refresh after failed MLD reconfiguration and use the resolved VAP interface for kernel state checks.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
